Measuring video playback on the C2 through the HDMI capture stick (docs/milestones.md
M15). All of them take the board's 1080p60 output as captured on this laptop.

  hdmi-record.sh <s> <out.mkv>     pauses tools/hdmi-live.sh, records <s>
                                   seconds at 60 fps (MJPEG as is), restarts it
  hdmi-record-av.sh <s> <out.mkv>  the same with the stick's HDMI audio
  tears.py <rec> <start> <s> <crop w:h:x:y>
                                   tears in the video area: a frame shown in
                                   two pieces in consecutive captures
  cadence.py <rec> <start> <s> <crop>
                                   gaps between changes of the video area, in
                                   captures (30 fps on 60 Hz: 2 each)
  avsync.py <rec> <crop>           audio offset of each white flash's beep
                                   (modulo the clip's 1 s marker period!)
  avsync-irregular.py <rec> <crop> the offset for the irregular clip below,
                                   whole seconds included
  bitsread.py <rec> <start> <s> <video w:h:x:y>
                                   the frame number each capture shows, for
                                   the bit box clip below: frames shown,
                                   how long each is held, skips, reversals

Test clips (a white frame and a 100 ms 1 kHz beep at the start of every
second; the second one is heavy to decode, like a phone video):
  ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "testsrc2=size=1280x720:rate=30,drawbox=enable='lt(mod(t\,1)\,0.0333)':color=white:t=fill" \
    -f lavfi -i "sine=frequency=1000:sample_rate=48000,volume=enable='gte(mod(t\,1)\,0.1)':volume=0" \
    -t 60 -c:v libx264 -profile:v high -pix_fmt yuv420p -b:v 6M -c:a aac avsync-720p.mp4
  ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "testsrc2=size=1080x1920:rate=30,noise=alls=25:allf=t,drawbox=enable='lt(mod(t\,1)\,0.0333)':color=white:t=fill" \
    -f lavfi -i "sine=frequency=1000:sample_rate=44100,volume=enable='gte(mod(t\,1)\,0.1)':volume=0" \
    -t 45 -c:v libx264 -preset fast -profile:v high -pix_fmt yuv420p -b:v 10M -c:a aac -ac 1 avsync-portrait.mp4

An irregular one (flash and beep at 2.0 3.4 5.9 7.1 10.6 12.2 15.8 17.3 20.9
23.4 25.0 28.7 s): build the enable expressions from that list as
"between(t,2.0,2.0333)+..." for drawbox and "not(between(t,2.0,2.1)+...)"
for the sine's volume, -t 32.

hdmi-record-av.sh stamps both inputs with the wall clock and keeps the time
stamps, so the files hold the real offset between picture and sound. The
capture path then shows sound 50 to 150 ms earlier than it was (the stick's
MJPEG frames arrive late), measured with KDL's screen switch and meson_hdmi's
test tone (media_server stopped). tools/probes/beepflash.cpp checks the
driver path the same way while streaming.

The bit box clip (milestone M31 (docs/milestones.md): the frame number as 11 boxes, white for a 1,
over testsrc2; cadence.py misses changes this small):
  b=""; for k in $(seq 0 10); do x=$((40 + k * 160)); b="$b,drawbox=x=$x:y=40:w=120:h=120:color=black:t=fill,drawbox=x=$x:y=40:w=120:h=120:color=white:t=fill:enable='eq(mod(floor(n/$((1<<k))),2),1)'"; done
  ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "testsrc2=size=1920x1080:rate=60$b" -t 20 -c:v libx265 \
    -preset fast -pix_fmt yuv420p -b:v 8M -tag:v hvc1 bits60.mp4
